i## title: A union filesystem in userspace	/	tilde.club	70
i## date: "2026-06-14"	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## Introduction	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iI find the various concepts and philosophy behind Plan 9	/	tilde.club	70
ivery interesting. About a month ago, I discovered the union	/	tilde.club	70
idirectory feature. It involves binding directories to other	/	tilde.club	70
idirectories. In practice, you end up with a directory that	/	tilde.club	70
ibehaves like a collection of directories. I wanted to try	/	tilde.club	70
iimplementing a similar feature for UNIX.	/	tilde.club	70
hPlan 9	URL:https://p9f.org/	p9f.org	443
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## My goal	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iThe main goal of this project is to have fun and learn about	/	tilde.club	70
itechnologies I wasn't familiar with. Technically, I'd like	/	tilde.club	70
ito write a virtual file system for UNIX that behaves	/	tilde.club	70
isimilarly to Plan 9's union dir. The idea is to have mount	/	tilde.club	70
ipoints that communicate with a daemon that manages a global	/	tilde.club	70
imount table. Having a client-server architecture will allow	/	tilde.club	70
ithe mount table to be managed even after the mount points	/	tilde.club	70
ihave been created.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## Implementation	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iSo, I decided to create a Python project on GitHub	/	tilde.club	70
icontaining a library and a CLI. The library provides Python	/	tilde.club	70
icode that communicates with FUSE to export a file system to	/	tilde.club	70
ithe kernel, a server to manage the global mount table in	/	tilde.club	70
imemory, and functions to communicate with that server. The	/	tilde.club	70
iCLI is a Python application that allows you to manage the	/	tilde.club	70
imount points of the virtual file system and manipulate the	/	tilde.club	70
iglobal mount table. Most of the file system operations are	/	tilde.club	70
iinspired by https://1e.iwp9.org/cready/unfs.pdf. For more	/	tilde.club	70
itechnical details, please refer to the project	/	tilde.club	70
idocumentation.	/	tilde.club	70
hPython project	URL:https://github.com/theobori/unionfs	github.com	443
hFUSE	URL:https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/next/filesystems/fuse.html	www.kernel.org	443
hhttps://1e.iwp9.org/cready/unfs.pdf	URL:https://1e.iwp9.org/cready/unfs.pdf	1e.iwp9.org	443
hproject documentation	URL:https://github.com/theobori/unionfs/blob/main/README.md	github.com	443
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## Components	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iBelow are the main components of the project.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### Mount Table	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iThe mount table is a Python object that manages a hash map,	/	tilde.club	70
iwhere each key is a path corresponding to a mount point, and	/	tilde.club	70
ieach value is a custom data structure designed to manage the	/	tilde.club	70
imounted directories. It has a time complexity of O(1) for	/	tilde.club	70
ieach required operation.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### Daemon	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iThis is a server that must be started before mounting the	/	tilde.club	70
ifilesystem. It is responsible for managing the global mount	/	tilde.club	70
itable in memory and handling mount and bind requests.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### Mount Points	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iThese export the filesystem to the kernel using FUSE. While	/	tilde.club	70
irunning, they communicate with the daemon to update their	/	tilde.club	70
ibound directories.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## Usage example	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iPersonally, I used it to organize Quake mods into a single	/	tilde.club	70
ifolder. I ran the commands below.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
imkdir -pv /tmp/union-quake	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iunionfs daemon --verbose	/	tilde.club	70
iunionfs mount /tmp/union-quake	/	tilde.club	70
iunionfs bind /tmp/union-quake ~/quake/ -a	/	tilde.club	70
iunionfs bind /tmp/union-quake ~/snacks/ -a	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
ivkquake -basedir /tmp/union-quake/	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iAnd I was able to play my Quake mods, which were spread out	/	tilde.club	70
iacross several folders.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## Project Progress	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iThe project is not entirely finished, there are still areas	/	tilde.club	70
ifor improvement to explore and tasks to complete. However,	/	tilde.club	70
iit remains functional.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## Conclusion	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iAlthough the project isn't quite finished yet, it was cool	/	tilde.club	70
ito create a small protocol dedicated to managing the mount	/	tilde.club	70
itable. I also got to explore FUSE in more detail and learn	/	tilde.club	70
isome new things. I'm pretty happy with the result.	/	tilde.club	70

